Never have more than four GitHub REST requests in flight. Before a GitHub job likely to make more than about 100 REST calls, run `gh api rate_limit`. Pause if the remaining core count is unknown. Stop if it is below 1,000. Send at most `min(4, remaining - 999)` REST calls per batch. Wait for each batch to finish and repeat the quota check before sending more. The check costs no primary quota. Allow one immediate quota check before work and after each completed batch. Wait at least a minute before each quota retry or repeat status poll.

Prefer one GraphQL query per repository over REST calls for individual pull requests. Prefer local Git (`git fetch`, `git log`, and `git merge-base`) over REST for questions about commits, ancestry, or merge methods. Prefer conditional requests when rereading a resource. Send its `ETag` with `If-None-Match`, or use `If-Modified-Since`. An authenticated 304 response costs no primary quota.
